{
  "id": "ep023",
  "duration": 45.909,
  "beats": [
    {
      "start": 0.08,
      "end": 3.721,
      "text": "Male deep-sea anglerfish dissolve their bodies to survive.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Caulophryne pelagica.jpg",
        "credit": "D. Shale",
        "license": "CC BY 2.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Caulophryne_pelagica.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 3.733,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 3.721,
      "end": 10.24,
      "text": "Starting with the scale of everyday fish, researchers found there are more than two hundred species of anglerfish.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "designed card"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 3.733,
          "end": 10.233,
          "kind": "designed",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 10.24,
      "end": 17.011,
      "text": "Moving up the ladder, females use a bioluminescent lure on their heads to attract unsuspecting prey.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Melanocetus johnsoni.png",
        "credit": "D. ROSS ROBERTSON, ARTURO ANGULO, CAROLE C. BALDWIN, DIANE PITASSY, AMY DRISKELL, LEE WEIGT, IGNACIO J.F. NAVARRO",
        "license": "CC BY 3.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Melanocetus_johnsoni.png"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 10.233,
          "end": 17.0,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 17.011,
      "end": 23.131,
      "text": "These massive females can stretch their jaws and stomachs to swallow prey up to twice their own size.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Melanocetus murrayi (Murrays abyssal anglerfish).jpg",
        "credit": "R. Mintern",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Melanocetus_murrayi_(Murrays_abyssal_anglerfish).jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 17.0,
          "end": 23.133,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 23.131,
      "end": 30.376,
      "text": "At the extreme end of the scale, female deep-sea anglerfish can grow up to sixty times the size of the tiny males.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "FMIB 52235 Caulophryne jordani Goode & Bean Gulf Stream Family Ceratiidae.jpeg",
        "credit": "David Starr Jordan",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:FMIB_52235_Caulophryne_jordani_Goode_%26_Bean_Gulf_Stream_Family_Ceratiidae.jpeg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 23.133,
          "end": 30.367,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 30.376,
      "end": 35.52,
      "text": "When a male finally encounters a female, he latches onto her using his teeth.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Ceratias uranoscopus.jpg",
        "credit": "Unknown author",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ceratias_uranoscopus.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 30.367,
          "end": 35.533,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 35.52,
      "end": 42.045,
      "text": "Over time, the attached male physically fuses with the female, merging their blood vessels and skin.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Cryptopsaras couesii.jpg",
        "credit": "Unknown author",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cryptopsaras_couesii.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 35.533,
          "end": 42.033,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 42.045,
      "end": 45.559,
      "text": "Male deep-sea anglerfish dissolve their bodies to survive.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Caulophryne pelagica.jpg",
